(the sidebar from feature 2 already linked here) with an honest
"coming soon" card explaining why the global list isn't live yet
and how to find audit history per-org in the meantime.

Files:
- src/app/[locale]/admin/audit/page.tsx — server route, SSG
  pre-renders for both locales.
- messages/{pl,en}.json — admin.audit namespace (title, subhead,
  placeholderTitle, placeholderBody, goToOrgs CTA).

Why a placeholder rather than a real list
=========================================
The identity-svc proto doesn't yet expose a global `ListAudit
Events` RPC. The audit_events table is already populated by
every admin mutation that ships in Slice 4 (block/unblock,
reset tokens, change plan, update org, update user, delete user),
but the only retrieval surface today is:

  identity.v1.IdentityService.AdminGetOrganization →
    OrganizationDetails.recent_audit (last 20 entries
    scoped to that org)

Building the global viewer requires a new backend RPC roughly:

  rpc AdminListAuditEvents(AdminListAuditEventsRequest)
    returns (AdminListAuditEventsResponse);

  AdminListAuditEventsRequest {
    int32 page_size = 1;
    string page_token = 2;
    string actor_email = 3;       // ILIKE, optional
    string action = 4;            // optional
    google.protobuf.Timestamp since = 5;  // optional
    google.protobuf.Timestamp until = 6;  // optional
  }

That's ~30 minutes of backend work (proto + sqlc query + handler).
Out of scope for the Slice-4-cont push; flagged for a follow-up.

In the meantime the placeholder page CTA links to /admin/orgs so
operators can drill into per-org audit panels via the org-detail
"Recent activity" card (Slice 4 feature 4).

